  bx('bl', "<b>Teacher on IR:</b> Britain 1750-1850, France 1870+, Germany 1870+ (British FDI), Japan 1868+, USA 1865+. For WEMC, India does IR only when Indian capitalists are strong, then pro-worker laws. Double hurt: govt not pro-Indian capitalist + raising costs (British firms can bear it)."),
  t("<b>Local Self-Government 1882</b> (Ripon 80-84 = Father of LSG)", "Goal: train Indians in self-government; key word <b>SELF</b>", "<b>Rural:</b> elected <b>District Boards</b>; electors = land-revenue payers (owners) + rent payers (tenants)", "<b>Urban:</b> municipalities, <b>at least two-thirds elected</b>, non-official chair", "Charge: <b>health, education, sanitation, roads, communications</b>; autonomy in daily work; govt keeps power to <b>inspect + dissolve</b>", "<b>Hunter Education Commission 1882-83</b>: education to local bodies, mass vernacular + female education; poor implementation", "Today: <b>Part IX</b> (Panchayati Raj) + <b>Part IX-A</b> (Municipalities), <b>73rd + 74th Amendments 1992</b>: 1882 seedling, 1992 tree", w=26),
  sec("THE ILBERT BILL 1883-84 " + P('2003') + P('2013'), 'r'),
  t("<b>Ilbert Bill</b> (most radicalising episode)", "Law Member <b>C.P. Ilbert</b>: Indian district judges to try Britons in mofussil", "Europeans organised, lobbied: <b>withdrawn + amended</b>; final = <b>mixed jury</b> in any case involving a Briton", "WEMC: British will not treat Indians as equals; <b>massive press campaigns</b>; max use of press by WEMC before 1885: here", "Teacher side note: Indian High Courts Act 1861, HCs in 1862 (M, B, C)", w=24),
  bx('ye', "<b>Traps:</b> Prelims 2003 (a) bring Indians + Europeans on par in criminal jurisdiction; (b) VPA 1878, (c) ICS-in-India demand (rejected), (d) Arms Act 1878. Prelims 2013 (c) removal of disqualification of Indian magistrates trying Europeans; (a) arms; (b) newspapers; (d) cotton duty irrelevant; board: WWI 1914-19."),
